figures.caption:
Figure 7: Crossing statistics under different realizations of the ISM density field and orbit integration. Each column corresponds to a different experiment.
Left column: fiducial simulation.
Middle column: identical setup, but with the ISM in the L20 map randomly shuffled within $|z|\leq 130$ pc, preserving the gas distribution while removing spatial correlations.
Right column: simulation with initial conditions chosen such that the Sun reaches heights where the vertical stratification of the disk changes significantly.
From top to bottom: projected L20 density map, with the horizontal lines marking the range of vertical oscillation ($z_{\odot}(t)$) sampled by the Solar System along its orbit;
$z$-distribution of the density bins encountered along the orbit (for all the orbit realizations performed);
measured residence time fraction (solid line), compared with the predicted one (dotted line) and the volume filling factor of the sampled region (dashed line);
median cloud crossing time as a function of density.
